      "description": "Watch Chelsea vs Luton highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. Under the lights at Stamford Bridge , Chelsea faced a determined Luton Town side in a cup tie that tested the patience and precision of the home favorites. Both sides sought a path to the next round, with the atmosphere buzzing as the first whistle blew. Frustration for the Blues in the Opening Half On August 27, 2026 , Chelsea looked to impose their will early on, dominating possession and carving out several high-quality openings. Cole Palmer was at the heart of everything, testing Luton Town goalkeeper Josh Keeley with multiple efforts in the first 15 minutes. Despite the creative spark from Estêvão and the constant pressure, the visitors held firm, relying on Keeley's sharp reflexes to keep the scores level. The woodwork proved to be the enemy for the hosts as the first half drew to a close. Morgan Rogers saw his powerful strike rattle the bar in the 44th minute after excellent work from Estêvão . While Luton had a rare chance through Hakeem Odoffin , whose header was saved by Mike Penders , the match remained goalless at the interval despite Chelsea's relentless offensive display. Welbeck Breaks the Deadlock as Chelsea Advance The breakthrough finally arrived five minutes into the second half. Malo Gusto delivered a pinpoint cross into the box, and Danny Welbeck rose highest to guide a header into the bottom left corner. The goal shifted the momentum further in Chelsea's favor, though they were denied a second shortly after when Cole Palmer's long-range effort struck the crossbar in the 64th minute. Chelsea eventually doubled their lead in the 79th minute under fortuitous circumstances when Hakeem Odoffin inadvertently turned the ball into his own net following a period of sustained pressure. Late drama saw Jamie Gittens hit the post and Luton's George Johnston miss a close-range header in stoppage time, but the damage was done. Chelsea secured their victory and safe passage to the next round of the Carabao Cup ."
